{"chunk_id":"R4-2500805-001","collection":"ran4_tdoc_chunks","metadata":{"source":["Samsung"],"tdocNumber":"R4-2500805","title":"Re-organize the 3Tx Notes and Release independence for 3Tx"},"point_id":"11316378890894940831"}
emaining open issues for inter-band ULCA/ENDC. One thing we would like to invite companies to discuss a bit is the 3Tx Notes in Table 6.2H.3.1-1 and Table 6.2L.3.1-1 of TS 38.101-1. Similarly for TS 38.101-3. The other is the release independency of 3Tx for handheld UE. The relevant agreements of last meetings are excerpted as following: In RAN4#112bis post meeting, draft big CR(R4-2414978) for HPUE was endorsed, and it has been noticed one new Note(i.e., Note 7) for 3Tx was added as following. From our understanding usually basket is supposed to commence after the discussion in general WI is finalized and necessary spec change is implemented. So the following spec change was removed as suggested by us during RAN4#113. As observed, so far there are already at least 4 Notes (i.e., Note 2,3,4,7) to indicate different “duplexer+MIMO” combination with different power class. It is expected more Notes would enter the spec if following current approach, we thing it is possible to re-organize these Notes and invite companies to think about it, the detailed wording can be discussed/decided based on the draft CRs led by CR author in future meeting, the following is just some inputs for CR leader’s consideration. Take Table 6.2H.3.1-1 to show our thinking. The information for the capable PC for each band is removed, considering for 2Tx inter-band CA, this kind of information is also not present in the spec but the corresponding TRs. The only indication left is which band can support UL-MIMO given the title of this Table is “…with UL MIMO in one frequency band”, we think this information might be helpful to better reflect operators’ demand thus instruct UE implementation. On the other hand, having UL MIMO capability in single band doesnot necessarily mean UE have to support UL MIMO in the band combinations. Anyway, we are open to discuss it, if companies think the indication of which band can support UL MIMO is unnecessary, it is ok to simply add general description right above the table to replace all these HPUE notes. Proposal 1: See conclusion part. Considering the implementation complexity and potential heat issue for handheld UE with 3Tx, we are not supportive 3Tx to have release independence attribute, which means 3Tx for handheld UE is from Rel-19 and no need to touch TS 38.307 for it at all. Proposal 2: 3Tx for handheld UE does not have release independence attribute.

